    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file, even though `frai-gate init --ci` (when run directly) does create it.\n\n**Root Cause:** In the frai CLI, the `--ci` flag is defined as a global option on the root `frai` program. When the user ran `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js consumed the `--ci` option at the root level before the gate subcommand's action handler was called. The gate command's action only received the variadic arguments `['init']` without the `--ci` flag, so it was never passed to the spawned `frai-gate` process.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the gate command's action handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Accept the `command` parameter (the Command object)\n2. Extract the parent program's options via `command.parent.optsWithGlobals()`\n3. Reconstruct all command-line arguments from both parent and command-level options\n4. Pass the complete argument list to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Updated `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to properly forward all options (including parent options) to the spawned frai-gate process\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Verified the fix works: `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
